WEBVTT

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:04.419
Read an old institutional email or academic abstract.

00:00:04.419 --> 00:00:04.638
You

00:00:04.638 --> 00:00:08.363
may find the immaculate, depersonalized language we

00:00:08.363 --> 00:00:08.582
now

00:00:08.582 --> 00:00:10.661
accuse machines of inventing.

00:00:16.842 --> 00:00:20.410
Universities demand standard structure, impeccable

00:00:20.410 --> 00:00:20.838
polish

00:00:20.838 --> 00:00:24.554
and phrases approved by gatekeepers. Writers learn to

00:00:24.554 --> 00:00:26.377
hide any particular voice.

00:00:32.258 --> 00:00:35.882
When software produces the very language institutions

00:00:35.882 --> 00:00:39.641
rewarded, people suddenly decide that the sound itself

00:00:39.641 --> 00:00:39.780
is

00:00:39.780 --> 00:00:40.737
incriminating.

00:00:46.092 --> 00:00:49.682
A sentence pattern is not evidence of who conceived an

00:00:49.682 --> 00:00:52.727
idea, performed an experiment or understood a

00:00:52.727 --> 00:00:53.471
conclusion.

00:00:58.217 --> 00:01:01.845
What does this author know? Are the sources real? Can

00:01:01.845 --> 00:01:02.050
the

00:01:02.050 --> 00:01:05.548
argument survive direct examination? Those questions

00:01:05.548 --> 00:01:06.691
require judgment.

00:01:12.008 --> 00:01:15.705
The essay is about intellectual responsibility, not an

00:01:15.705 --> 00:01:19.266
entitlement to publish inaccuracies in a distinctive

00:01:19.266 --> 00:01:19.676
style.
